# Frontend structure

`web/` is React + Vite (npm only). `moduleResolution: bundler`, so a bare
directory import resolves to its `index.{ts,tsx}` — use barrels.

## `web/src/` layout

```
src/
├── api/         # HTTP client + endpoint modules (barrel: api/index.ts)
│   └── client.ts
├── types/       # shared TS types (barrel: types/index.ts)
├── store/       # global store: Provider + domain hooks (see below)
├── lib/         # framework-free utils (lib/format.ts)
├── hooks/       # custom hooks (useStore stays with its Provider in store/)
├── components/  # shared only — used by ≥2 pages or by Shell/App
├── pages/       # route-level pages; page-private components live here
│   └── TeachPage/
│       ├── index.tsx
│       ├── index.module.scss
│       └── SomeWidget/          # page-private: PascalCase folder
│           ├── index.tsx
│           └── index.module.scss
├── assets/      # static assets
├── App.tsx
├── main.tsx
└── global.scss
```

## Rules

- **No flat root files** for api/types/store/format — they live in their
  named directories with a barrel `index`. Import as `from "../api"`,
  `from "../types"`, `from "../store"`; the barrel resolves.
- `api/` holds the HTTP client (`api`, `uploadFile`, `fetchBlob` in
  `client.ts`) and, when endpoint helpers accrete, one file per subdomain
  (`day.ts`, `drill.ts`, `resume.ts`, …) re-exported from `api/index.ts`.
  Components call endpoints through these, not raw `fetch`.
- `store/` owns the global context. Keep **one** `StoreProvider` + `useStore`
  for callers; do not split into multiple Contexts. Internals are domain hooks
  aligned with backend subdomains:
  ```
  store/
  ├── index.tsx       # StoreProvider assembles hooks → one Store value
  ├── types.ts        # Store (+ ChatTurn, Run)
  ├── useShell.ts     # mode / busy / flash / error / menus + bindRun
  ├── useWorkspace.ts # day snapshot + refresh (plan/notes/projects/resume/drill lists)
  ├── useNotes.ts
  ├── useProject.ts
  ├── useExamine.ts
  ├── useTeach.ts
  └── useDrill.ts
  ```
  `useStore` stays here (not in `hooks/`) because it is bound to this Provider.
- `lib/` is framework-free pure utils (date/format/html helpers). No React
  imports here.
- `hooks/` is for reusable React hooks shared across components. A hook
  coupled to a single Provider stays with that Provider.
- **Shared vs page-private components:**
  - `components/<Name>/` — only if used by Shell/App or by **two or more**
    pages. Same two-file rule: `index.tsx` + `index.module.scss` (CSS Modules,
    no global class names).
  - `pages/<Name>Page/<Child>/` — if a component is only used by one page,
    put it under that page as a PascalCase subfolder with the same two files.
    Import as `from "./Child"`. Do **not** leave page-private UI in
    `components/`.
  - A shared component’s private helper may live as a sibling under
    `components/` (e.g. `YuqueNoteEditor` used only by `NoteComposeModal`).
- `pages/<Name>Page/` is the route shell (`index.tsx` + optional
  `index.module.scss`) plus any page-private child folders.
- Keep subdomain naming aligned with the backend (`day`, `note`, `drill`,
  `resume`, `project`, `memory`, `prompt`) so frontend `api/<domain>.ts`
  maps 1:1 to backend `api/routes/<domain>.py` + `db.ops/<domain>.py`.

## When adding a feature

1. Types → `types/index.ts` (or a domain file re-exported by the barrel).
2. Endpoint helper → `api/<domain>.ts` (re-export from `api/index.ts`); fall
   back to `api<T>("/v1/...")` inline only for one-off calls.
3. Store state/actions → matching `store/use<Domain>.ts` (wire in
   `store/index.tsx`); shared lists that `refresh` loads go in `useWorkspace`.
4. Reusable hook → `hooks/`.
5. UI: shared → `components/<Name>/`; page-only → `pages/<Name>Page/<Name>/`.
6. Page shell → `pages/<Name>Page/` (`index.tsx` + `index.module.scss`).
